  "released": "2026-08-26",
  "changelog": "v223: receipts, the fold, and the promoted source \u2014 truth you can rebuild (wave B, items B1 and B2 of the audited final timeline build plan, \u00a74.2 and \u00a74.1). WHY: v220 froze what a temporal interpretation IS; nothing yet put one on disk, and a claim substrate whose active set cannot be reconstructed from its evidence is not a substrate \u2014 it is a cache with opinions. ONE NEW MODULE, `system/temporal_store.py`, and one invariant it exists to make true: DELETE THE ACTIVE INDEX, REBUILD IT FROM THE CHECKED-IN RECEIPTS, GET THE SAME BYTES. `fold_active_index` is a pure function of what is on disk \u2014 no clock, no model, no iteration-order luck, and deliberately NO `generated_at` field, because a timestamp inside a rebuildable artifact is a byte that cannot be reproduced and therefore a lie about what \u2018identical\u2019 means. A randomized property test shuffles the order the same evidence is written in and demands byte-identical output, because \u2018deterministic\u2019 that only holds for the order the author happened to try is not deterministic. THE RECEIPT STORE IS IMMUTABLE. A receipt is published once at v220's derived path (source key / revision / extractor); re-running the SAME extractor over the SAME revision writes nothing, and re-running a DIFFERENT extractor writes a NEW receipt beside the old one \u2014 a later model reading the same prose is a new interpretation, never a cache rebuild, and yesterday's reading stays on disk with its provenance intact. Rewriting an existing receipt's bytes is the one thing this store calls corruption (`receipt_immutable_conflict`). NOTHING IS EVER DELETED. The fold picks the latest receipt per (source, revision), keeps the losing interpretation's claims with status `superseded`, applies `supersedes_claim_ids` from winning receipts only, and applies corrections \u2014 and every retired claim keeps its full record plus the MARKS that explain it. Status is resolved as the STRONGEST mark over an unordered set (retracted > superseded > disputed > active), never \u2018last writer wins\u2019, which is what makes the answer independent of discovery order. A correction naming an unknown claim is reported, not swallowed; a receipt that will not parse is reported, not skipped. CORRECTIONS ARE SOURCES, NOT STATE. `supersede_claims` / `retract_claims` / `dispute_claims` file a durable markdown source under `sources/corrections/` whose filename is a pure function of what it says, so the same correction filed twice is one record. A correction says only which claims stop standing and why; saying what is true INSTEAD is a separate traceable act \u2014 promote the correcting words as a source and file a receipt over them \u2014 which keeps the replacement as provenanced as the claim it replaces and keeps the record free of a circular self-citation. OPTION B, BUILT (owner amendment 2). `promote_conversational_source` files a claim-bearing message as an ordinary vault source under the new `sources/conversations/` before anything cites it, so no claim's only citation is a session row. It is idempotent on the utterance's identity \u2014 the words plus session and turn, never the wall clock or the channel \u2014 and one message with N facts is promoted ONCE while every claim cites the same revision, which is the source's own content digest. THE PAIRING RULE: source first, then receipt, both idempotent, so a crash between them leaves a re-runnable state and NEVER a receipt citing a source that is not in the vault (`file_message_extraction` does both in order; `write_receipt` refuses the reverse by name). Registered in `vault_contract.json` (contract v8): `sources/conversations`, `state/temporal_claims`, its `receipts/` tree and `active-index.json`. The store deliberately imports neither `lifehug_core` nor `source_integrity` \u2014 their import BINDS the interpreter to one vault root and this API is told which vault on every call \u2014 so the shared frontmatter emitter is reimplemented and pinned byte-identical by a parity test. Constraint folding, person resolution and the calculated timeline remain waves C and D.",
